# po-triage-20260825T1345Z-mint.jq — PO triage batch mint, 2026-08-25T13:45Z cycle.
#
# Owning flow doc: docs/agents/po/flow/triage-signals.md (mint discipline) +
#                  docs/agents/po/flow/main.md § Reusable triage scripts
# Registry pointer: docs/agents/po/flow/scripts-registry.md
#
# Usage (NEVER raw mv/cp/> — CLAUDE.md § Orch-State Hot File Write Contract):
#   jq -f scripts/po-triage-20260825T1345Z-mint.jq docs/data/orch/orch-state.json \
#     | bash scripts/orch-apply.sh
#
# Idempotent: every append is guarded on the row id not already existing in backlog[].
# status MUST be "BACKLOG" (LANE_ALLOWED_STATUSES.backlog = {BACKLOG, BLOCKED}).

def add_row($row):
  if ([.task_board.backlog[] | select(.id == $row.id)] | length) > 0
  then .
  else .task_board.backlog += [$row]
  end;

("2026-08-25T13:45:50Z") as $now
| ("po/triage-20260825T1345Z") as $by

# ── 1. THE row that actually captures the user's BCTC-quality goal ────────────
| add_row({
    id: "FIX-PDFX-TESSERACT-CONFIDENCE-MEAN-OVER-NONEMPTY-MASKS-TOTAL-PAGE-MISS",
    type: "FIX", size: "S", priority: "P1", status: "BACKLOG",
    zone: "apps/pdf-extractor/", owner: "po", next_agent: "dev-pdf-extractor",
    created_at: $now, created_by: $by, updated_at: $now, updated_by: "po",
    dedup_key: "pdfx-ocr:tesseract-confidence-mean-over-nonempty-rows",
    files: ["apps/pdf-extractor/infrastructure/ocr_backends.py"],
    title: "TesseractVieBackend reports confidence as mean(conf) over ONLY the rows it managed to recognise, so a page it almost entirely MISSED self-reports high confidence — this is why AutoFallbackOcrBackend's 0.5 threshold never fires and `auto` mode is byte-identical to tesseract-vie on 30/30 units",
    root_cause: "apps/pdf-extractor/infrastructure/ocr_backends.py, TesseractVieBackend.recognize_text(): `valid_rows = data[(data['conf'] > 0) & (data['text'].str.strip() != '')]` then `mean_conf = float(valid_rows['conf'].mean()) / 100.0`. The denominator is the SUCCESSFULLY-RECOGNISED rows, not the rows that should have been recognised. A page where tesseract picks up three header words at conf 92 and loses all forty data rows therefore returns 0.92 — indistinguishable from a clean full-page read. Recall is invisible to the score by construction; only precision-on-what-was-found is measured. PO re-derived this at source 2026-08-25, independent of the reporting specialist.",
    evidence: "Measured by dev-pdf-extractor on FPT Q4 2025 (report_id e71f845d-ffa5-48f9-8f09-30ac2cd09c65, 46 pages), 4 real sentinel extractions in ephemeral `docker compose run --rm` containers, zero code changes, every result verified by direct readonly bun:sqlite row counts against market.db (NOT push-handler echo). OCR_TEXT_BACKEND=auto produced output BYTE-IDENTICAL to tesseract-vie on all 30/30 table units INCLUDING page 9 — the rescue never fired even once. Page 9 (quarterly income statement) is the proof case: tesseract extracted headers plus a stray '178%' and lost 100% of the revenue/profit figures, while PaddleOCR on the same page returned the full row correctly. So a genuine catastrophic per-page miss exists, a working rescue backend exists, and the confidence signal is the ONLY thing standing between them.",
    ac: "(AC-1) Confidence must fall on a near-total page miss. Build a discriminator that accounts for what was NOT recognised — candidates to evaluate and choose between explicitly: recognised-area / table-region-area coverage ratio; recognised row count vs the row count the layout detector found in the same region; mean(conf) weighted by character count with a floor for empty regions. Do not simply lower the 0.5 threshold — that trades one arbitrary constant for another and is an automatic rejection. (AC-2) POSITIVE CONTROL, mandatory and non-substitutable: re-run FPT Q4 2025 page 9 under OCR_TEXT_BACKEND=auto and show the rescue FIRES and the revenue/profit figures land. A unit test on synthetic input does not satisfy this. (AC-3) NEGATIVE CONTROL: re-run the other 29 units under auto and show the rescue does NOT fire on any of them — a discriminator that rescues everything reintroduces PaddleOCR's diacritic regression fleet-wide (see PO ruling in docs/agent-memory/decisions/triage-20260825T1345Z-po.md) and is a rejection. (AC-4) Report the auto-mode wall-clock and peak ru_maxrss for the corrected run; the table phase must stay under the 2.5 GiB per-container cap with the same headroom tesseract-vie has today (peak 1543 MiB, ~60%).",
    status_note: "PO RULING 2026-08-25: this row — not a backend swap — is the correct response to the standing 'improve BCTC extraction quality' goal. PaddleOCR adoption was measured and REJECTED (it strips Vietnamese diacritics on nearly every word, runs 1.8x slower, and peaks at 2790 MiB against a 2560 MiB cap). PaddleOCR's single genuine win was page 9, and `auto` already has the mechanism to capture exactly that win without paying the diacritic regression — it is only the confidence signal that is broken. Full ruling + method + what would reopen the backend question: docs/agent-memory/decisions/triage-20260825T1345Z-po.md.",
    dedup_checked: "2026-08-25T13:40Z via scripts/po-board-dedup-search.sh over NON-TERMINAL lanes and --all-lanes for /TesseractVie|AutoFallback|confidence.*heuristic|mean.*conf/ and /paddle|PaddleOCR|tesseract|OCR/ and /PEK-IMPL-OCR|ocr.?backend|OCR_BACKEND/. No row on any lane covers the confidence heuristic or the backend-selection question. Nearest neighbours read and rejected: PERF-PEK-PER-PAGE-LATENCY (throughput, not quality), FIX-BCTC-REFINE-DIACRITIC-COLLAPSE-A-BREVE-ACUTE (refine-stage diacritic collapse downstream of OCR), FIX-PDFX-GENERIC-MD-TABLE-OCR-UNROUTED-GATEWAY (a different extractor's pytesseract call sites).",
    related: ["FIX-PDFX-PEK-TABLE-REGION-COLLAPSED-TO-ONE-CELL-DISCARDS-PER-LINE-BBOXES", "FIX-BCTC-REFINE-DIACRITIC-COLLAPSE-A-BREVE-ACUTE"],
    baseline_pass: null
  })

# ── 2. Structural table-flattening regression, ALL backends, since PEK-IMPL-OCR ─
| add_row({
    id: "FIX-PDFX-PEK-TABLE-REGION-COLLAPSED-TO-ONE-CELL-DISCARDS-PER-LINE-BBOXES",
    type: "FIX", size: "M", priority: "P1", status: "BACKLOG",
    zone: "apps/pdf-extractor/", owner: "po", next_agent: "architect",
    created_at: $now, created_by: $by, updated_at: $now, updated_by: "po",
    dedup_key: "pdfx-pek:table-region-single-cell-discards-per-line-bboxes",
    files: ["apps/pdf-extractor/infrastructure/pek_engine_adapter.py", "apps/pdf-extractor/infrastructure/ocr_backends.py"],
    title: "Since PEK-IMPL-OCR the pluggable OCR path wraps an ENTIRE table region into ONE cell dict carrying the whole-region bbox, so per-line bboxes are discarded and table row/column structure is flattened for EVERY backend, tesseract included — the legacy paddle_table path it replaced did preserve them",
    root_cause: "apps/pdf-extractor/infrastructure/pek_engine_adapter.py, _run_table_extraction (~lines 1146-1165). When `self._ocr_backend is not None` — which is the live configuration for every backend value of OCR_TEXT_BACKEND — the code calls `self._ocr_backend.recognize_text(crop)` on the whole cropped table region and appends exactly ONE cell: `{bbox: [x0, y0, x1, y1], text: cell_text, score: cell_score}`. That bbox is the REGION bbox, not a line bbox, and cell_text is every recognised line joined into a single string. The `else` branch — the backward-compatible path taken only when no backend is injected — calls `paddle_table.ocr(crop, cls=False)` and iterates the per-line results, which is where the structure used to come from. So the pluggable-backend refactor silently traded table structure for backend pluggability, and _assemble_unit_markdown / _cells_to_row_bands downstream receive one band per region regardless of how many rows the table actually has. PO re-derived this at source 2026-08-25.",
    evidence: "Read directly from apps/pdf-extractor/infrastructure/pek_engine_adapter.py at the cited lines: the `if self._ocr_backend is not None` branch appends a single dict whose bbox is the same [x0, y0, x1, y1] used to make the crop. Corroborated behaviourally by dev-pdf-extractor's 2026-08-25 sentinel run: OCR_TEXT_BACKEND=auto and OCR_TEXT_BACKEND=tesseract-vie produced BYTE-IDENTICAL output on 30/30 table units, which is only possible if the downstream assembly is insensitive to per-line geometry. This is a strictly larger quality lever for BCTC than the backend choice was, and it is why a backend swap could never have delivered the goal on its own.",
    ac: "(AC-1) Decide and record the contract before touching code: does OcrBackendPort return (text, confidence) or a list of (bbox, text, confidence) lines? The current port signature is the actual root cause — it cannot express what the caller needs — so a fix that keeps the signature and reconstructs geometry downstream must be argued for explicitly, not defaulted into. (AC-2) All three backends (TesseractVieBackend, PaddleOcrBackend, AutoFallbackOcrBackend) must satisfy the chosen contract; a fix that only restores structure for paddle re-creates the exact asymmetry this row is about. (AC-3) POSITIVE CONTROL on real data, not fixtures: extract a known multi-row BCTC table (FPT Q4 2025, report_id e71f845d-ffa5-48f9-8f09-30ac2cd09c65) and show the produced markdown has one row per source row, verified by direct readonly bun:sqlite query against market.db, never by a push-handler echo. (AC-4) Regression fence: assert the legacy `else` branch and the pluggable branch now produce the same row COUNT on the same region — the two paths silently diverging is the defect class itself.",
    status_note: "Routed to architect, not developer: AC-1 is a port-contract decision across three adapters plus two downstream assemblers, not a local edit. Found during the PaddleOCR adoption measurement 2026-08-25; it is pre-existing and independent of that decision — it affects tesseract-vie, which is and remains the live backend.",
    dedup_checked: "2026-08-25T13:40Z via scripts/po-board-dedup-search.sh for /_run_table_extraction|pek_engine_adapter|combined.?text|per-line bbox/ -> NO MATCH on non-terminal lanes, and /PEK-IMPL-OCR|ocr.?backend|OCR_BACKEND|backend swap|ocr engine/ --all-lanes -> NO MATCH on any lane.",
    related: ["FIX-PDFX-TESSERACT-CONFIDENCE-MEAN-OVER-NONEMPTY-MASKS-TOTAL-PAGE-MISS", "SPIKE-BCTC-COLUMN-SEPARATED-LAYOUT", "FIX-BCTC-FPT-PAGE8-EPS-BLEED-ROWCOUNT"],
    baseline_pass: null
  })

# ── 3. Market-hours guard covers 1 of 5 OCR-driving routes ────────────────────
| add_row({
    id: "FIX-PDFX-MARKET-HOURS-GUARD-ONLY-ON-PEK-EXTRACT-FOUR-OCR-ROUTES-UNGUARDED",
    type: "FIX", size: "S", priority: "P2", status: "BACKLOG",
    zone: "apps/pdf-extractor/", owner: "po", next_agent: "dev-pdf-extractor",
    created_at: $now, created_by: $by, updated_at: $now, updated_by: "po",
    dedup_key: "pdfx-market-hours-guard:only-pek-extract-route-guarded",
    files: ["apps/pdf-extractor/interface/routes_pek.py", "apps/pdf-extractor/interface/routes_extract.py", "apps/pdf-extractor/interface/routes_extract_tables.py", "apps/pdf-extractor/interface/routes_md_tables.py", "apps/pdf-extractor/interface/routes_layout_first.py"],
    title: "The VN market-hours 503 guard is wired into exactly ONE of the five OCR-driving routes — /extract, /extract-tables, /extract-md-tables and /extract-layout-first can all start a multi-GiB OCR burst during market hours on a container that already runs at 88-98% of its 2.5 GiB cap",
    root_cause: "is_vn_market_open_utc() is imported and called at apps/pdf-extractor/interface/routes_pek.py:17 and :64 and NOWHERE else in apps/pdf-extractor outside __tests__/ and scenarios/. PO enumerated every registered route: routes_pek.py:29 /pek-extract (GUARDED), routes_extract.py:36 /extract, routes_extract_tables.py:22 /extract-tables, routes_md_tables.py:55 /extract-md-tables, routes_layout_first.py:56 /extract-layout-first (all UNGUARDED), plus /page-text, /rasterize, /health which do not drive OCR. The guard was added for REQ-PEK-11 / AC-PEK-NEW-1 against the pek route only and was never swept across the sibling routes that reach the same engine.",
    evidence: "grep -rn 'is_vn_market_open_utc' apps/pdf-extractor -> 1 production call site (routes_pek.py:64). Route enumeration by grep over @router.post/@router.get across apps/pdf-extractor/interface/ -> 8 routes, 5 OCR-driving, 1 guarded. Pre-existing, not introduced by any 2026-08-25 change. Impact is real and already-measured on this container: FIX-PDFX-PARENT-PROCESS-MEMORY-BURST-HEADROOM (review[]) and FIX-AUDITOR-EMIT-SEVERITY-LABEL-FLAT-ESCALATION-BYPASS-NEVER-FIRES both record pdf-extractor at 88-98.87% of its 2.5 GiB cap under ordinary traffic.",
    ac: "(AC-1) Every OCR-driving route honours the same market-hours policy as /pek-extract, applied through ONE shared dependency/middleware — five copies of the same `if` is a rejection, it is the exact copy-paste-drift shape that produced this gap. (AC-2) The three non-OCR routes (/page-text, /rasterize, /health) must stay UNGUARDED and a test must assert that — guarding /health would break the container healthcheck and cause restart churn. (AC-3) Test coverage mirrors apps/pdf-extractor/__tests__/test_market_hours_guard.py for each newly-guarded route: 503 inside market hours, 202/200 outside, with is_vn_market_open_utc patched at its definition module (see routes_pek.py:8-9 on why the patch target must not be indirected). (AC-4) Enumerate the callers of the four routes before changing them and name any that would newly receive a 503 during market hours; a caller that breaks is a scoping question for PO, not a silent regression.",
    status_note: "Found while measuring the OCR backend question 2026-08-25; unrelated to that decision. P2 rather than P1: it is a latent capacity risk with no recorded incident yet, but the container's measured headroom makes it a plausible OOM trigger.",
    dedup_checked: "2026-08-25T13:40Z via scripts/po-board-dedup-search.sh for /is_vn_market_open_utc|routes_pek|market-hours guard/ -> NO MATCH on non-terminal board rows.",
    related: ["FIX-PDFX-PARENT-PROCESS-MEMORY-BURST-HEADROOM", "FIX-PDFX-PRECURSOR-TELEMETRY-98PCT-VMHWM-PINNED-15MIN-BEFORE-THE-OOM-KILL"],
    baseline_pass: null
  })

# ── 4. task_release Rung B is inert — PROBED, with control ────────────────────
| add_row({
    id: "FIX-TASKRELEASE-ORIGINAL-OWNER-CLIENT-SESSION-INERT-RUNGB-NEVER-RELEASES",
    type: "FIX", size: "S", priority: "P0", status: "BACKLOG",
    zone: "cross-service/", owner: "po", next_agent: "architect",
    created_at: $now, created_by: $by, updated_at: $now, updated_by: "po",
    dedup_key: "tasklock:task-release-original-owner-client-session-param-inert",
    files: ["docs/agents/dev-team/flow/orphan-adoption.md", "apps/mcp-server/src/interface/mcp/tools/"],
    title: "task_release's original_owner_client_session parameter grants NO release authority — PO probed it live with a positive control: the FR-2 Rung B call shape returns released:0 and leaves the lock held, while releasing under the dead session's own id returns released:1. All 3 orphan-signal release call sites are therefore permanently no-ops, and FIX-ORPHAN-FR4-FR5 subtask 4 is unsatisfiable as written",
    root_cause: "task_release authorises solely on owner_client_session matching the lock's own owner_client_session. original_owner_client_session is accepted by the schema and then ignored. The FR-2 Rung B design assumed the server would treat it as a delegated-release credential; it does not. The doc-side half of subtask 4 DID land — docs/agents/dev-team/flow/orphan-adoption.md :61-66, :128-136 and :169-174 all now pass owner_agent + original_owner_client_session — so the row looks complete on inspection while remaining functionally dead, which is why 15 days of review never caught it.",
    evidence: "PO live probe 2026-08-25T13:52Z via mcp__gateway__call_tool(server='vn-market'), full sequence: (1) task_claim(task_id='orphan-signal:PO-SYNTHETIC-FR2-RUNGB-PROBE-20260825', task_kind='orphan-signal', owner_agent='dev-team', owner_client_session='dead-session-00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000') -> {claimed:true}. (2) TEST — the exact orphan-adoption.md:61-66 shape: task_release(task_id=<same>, owner_client_session='036ceaf1-...' (the CALLER), owner_agent='dev-team', original_owner_client_session='dead-session-...') -> {ok:true, released:0}. (3) task_list_held(kind='orphan-signal') -> count:1, lock STILL HELD — released:0 is a genuine non-release, not an already-gone no-op. (4) POSITIVE CONTROL — same lock, owner_client_session='dead-session-...' (the lock's own owner): -> {ok:true, released:1}. (5) task_list_held(kind='orphan-signal') -> count:0, clean, no probe residue. The control proves release itself works and isolates the fault to Rung B specifically. This FALSIFIES the standing note feedback_orphan_signal_unreleasable_null_client_session_and_activesprints_only_flip, which recorded that orphan-signals ARE releasable by passing owner_agent + original_owner_client_session.",
    ac: "(AC-1) Choose ONE and record why in a brief before editing: (a) CALLER-SIDE — change the 3 call sites in docs/agents/dev-team/flow/orphan-adoption.md to pass `owner_client_session: dead_session` (the value is already in scope at all 3 sites, it is currently being passed as original_owner_client_session), which the control above proves works today with zero server change; or (b) SERVER-SIDE — implement original_owner_client_session as a real delegated-release credential. (b) is the larger blast radius: it makes any caller able to release any lock by naming its owner, so it needs an argued authorisation story, not just an OR in the WHERE clause. (AC-2) Replay the exact 5-step probe above and show step (2) now returns released:1 with the lock gone at step (3). A unit test does not satisfy this — the defect is server behaviour reached through the gateway. (AC-3) If (a) is chosen, task_release's original_owner_client_session parameter must be removed from the tool schema or documented as inert in docs/standards/mcp-tools.md — leaving an accepted-and-ignored parameter in place is what manufactured this false-green. (AC-4) FIX-ORPHAN-FR4-FR5-FLOW-DEVTEAM-ADOPTION-GUARD subtask 4's acceptance must be restated as a SYNTHETIC-fixture probe (claim a throwaway orphan-signal under a dead session, then release it) — its current wording requires 'a real NULL-owner orphan-signal row', and PO measured task_list_held(kind='orphan-signal') = 0 live rows, so as written it can only be satisfied opportunistically after a genuine mid-task agent death. That is a structural stall on a P0, not an acceptance criterion.",
    status_note: "P0 because it blocks FIX-ORPHAN-FR4-FR5-FLOW-DEVTEAM-ADOPTION-GUARD (P0, review[], QA CHANGES_REQUESTED) and because a permanently-no-op orphan release means every adopted orphan-signal leaks its lock until TTL expiry. Routed to architect for the AC-1 caller-vs-server decision, which must be made before any file is touched.",
    dedup_checked: "2026-08-25T13:50Z via scripts/po-board-dedup-search.sh for /ORPHAN-FR4|FR-4|FR-5|orphan.*signal.*released/ and /dispatch-claim|FR-3|CARD\\.md/ -> the only related open row is FIX-ORPHAN-FR4-FR5-FLOW-DEVTEAM-ADOPTION-GUARD (review[26]), which is the CONSUMER of this fix, not a duplicate of it: that row owns the flow-doc changes, this row owns the release-authorisation mechanism its subtask 4 depends on.",
    related: ["FIX-ORPHAN-FR4-FR5-FLOW-DEVTEAM-ADOPTION-GUARD", "FIX-DISPATCHCLAIM-CARD-PAYLOAD-OBJECT-REJECTED-AND-PHASEA-OMITS-OWNER-AGENT"],
    baseline_pass: null
  })

