| add_row({
    id: "FIX-DISPATCHCLAIM-CARD-PAYLOAD-OBJECT-REJECTED-AND-PHASEA-OMITS-OWNER-AGENT",
    type: "FIX", size: "S", priority: "P1", status: "BACKLOG",
    zone: "cross-service/", owner: "po", next_agent: "agent-father",
    created_at: $now, created_by: $by, updated_at: $now, updated_by: "po",
    dedup_key: "dispatch-claim-card:payload-object-and-missing-owner-agent",
    files: [".claude/skills/dispatch-claim/CARD.md", ".claude/skills/dispatch-claim/SKILL.md"],
    title: "dispatch-claim/CARD.md — the router's hot-path card, executed before EVERY spawn — shows task_claim payload as a JSON OBJECT at both Phase A and Phase B, but the live tool requires a serialized STRING; Phase A additionally omits owner_agent, which the schema marks required. Both make the card's copy-executable snippets fail as written",
    root_cause: ".claude/skills/dispatch-claim/CARD.md:17 (Phase A) and :29 (Phase B) both write `payload={...}`. The live vn-market task_claim schema declares payload as a string. CARD.md:16-17 also calls task_claim with task_id/task_kind/owner_client_session/ttl/payload and NO owner_agent, which the schema marks required (Phase B at :28 does pass it). docs/agents/dev-team/flow/drain-signals.md already documents the string form correctly — CARD.md is the stale copy, and it is the one the router actually reads on the hot path.",
    evidence: "PO probed the live schema 2026-08-25T13:47Z via mcp__gateway__call_tool(server='vn-market', tool='task_claim') with payload passed as an object. The server returned a Zod validation error naming three problems at once: path ['payload'] {expected:'string', received:'object'}, path ['owner_agent'] {expected:'string', received:'undefined', message:'Required'}, and the task_kind enum (which is exactly ['cowork-slot','sprint-task','dashboard-row','commit-mutex','intent','orphan-signal','session-presence'] — CARD.md does not enumerate it). Not relayed: PO made the call and read the error. CORRECTION RECORDED FOR THE IMPLEMENTER, do not 'fix' this too: CARD.md:11's `task_list_held(kind=...)` is CORRECT — PO separately verified that task_list_held filters on `kind` (kind='cowork-slot' -> 4 locks) and silently IGNORES `task_kind` (task_kind='zzz-nonexistent' -> all 13 locks, identical to unfiltered). The input parameter is `kind` while the response field is `task_kind`; that asymmetry is a real ergonomics trap but the card is on the right side of it.",
    ac: "(AC-1) Both payload sites become serialized JSON strings, and Phase A gains owner_agent. (AC-2) The corrected snippets are EXECUTED once each against the live gateway and the result pasted into the commit message — this card is copy-executable by construction, so inspection is not acceptance. (AC-3) Sweep, do not point-fix: grep every skill/flow doc for `payload={` or `payload = {` on a task_claim/task_heartbeat line and fix the whole set; report the count. (AC-4) Same row also carries the dispatch-claim/SKILL.md FR-3 retrofit that FIX-ORPHAN-FR4-FR5-FLOW-DEVTEAM-ADOPTION-GUARD's record claims exists as a 'separate row' — PO grep-verified 2026-08-25 that no such row existed anywhere on board or archive. This row is now that row; the FR-3 retrofit is in scope here and the reference in that record resolves to this id.",
    status_note: "P1 despite being a doc change: CARD.md is on the router's pre-spawn hot path (CLAUDE.md § BEFORE spawning any agent, step 2.5) and a router that follows it literally gets a hard validation error instead of a claim. Routed to agent-father per the 2026-07-21 PO artifact-class routing ruling — .claude/skills/** is instruction-prose an agent loads and executes.",
    dedup_checked: "2026-08-25T13:50Z via scripts/po-board-dedup-search.sh for /dispatch-claim|FR-3|CARD\\.md/ -> 6 hits, all read and rejected: UC-RDL-P4B-DOC-CUTOVER (FR-7 dispatch_preflight cutover, a different retrofit), STYLE-SKILL-FRONTMATTER-ALIGN (YAML frontmatter), FIX-PO-MANUAL-DISPATCH-SKIP-STAMP-FIELD-MISMATCH, FIX-CHEF-INTRADAY-MARKER-KEY-UTC-HOUR-BASIS-MIGRATION, FIX-REENTRANT-BRANCH-SHARED-SESSION-UUID-DOUBLE-DISPATCH, FIX-ORCH-SENTINEL-OH4. None is about the payload type or a missing owner_agent.",
    related: ["FIX-ORPHAN-FR4-FR5-FLOW-DEVTEAM-ADOPTION-GUARD", "UC-RDL-P4B-DOC-CUTOVER", "FIX-TASKRELEASE-ORIGINAL-OWNER-CLIENT-SESSION-INERT-RUNGB-NEVER-RELEASES"],
