# ── 6. A-30 debounce keyed on container NAME ──────────────────────────────────
| add_row({
    id: "FIX-AUDITOR-A30-DEBOUNCE-KEYED-ON-CONTAINER-NAME-EPHEMERAL-UNBOUNDED-CARDINALITY",
    type: "FIX", size: "S", priority: "P1", status: "BACKLOG",
    zone: "apps/mcp-server/", owner: "po", next_agent: "developer",
    created_at: $now, created_by: $by, updated_at: $now, updated_by: "po",
    dedup_key: "auditor:a30-mem-creep|defect:no-ephemeral-container-discriminator",
    files: ["docs/agents/system-auditor/probe.sh", "docs/data/auditor-tier1-spawn-debounce.json"],
    title: "A-30 mem_creep has no ephemeral-container discriminator and its spawn debounce is keyed on container NAME, so every `docker compose run --rm` container is a brand-new key and therefore a guaranteed first-sighting SPAWN — 3 distinct throwaway names paged the auditor in 13 minutes",
    root_cause: "The tier-1 spawn debounce ledger (docs/data/auditor-tier1-spawn-debounce.json) records first_seen_at/spawn_count per container NAME. Names produced by `docker compose run --rm` are generated per invocation and never repeat, so their key cardinality is unbounded and the debounce can never suppress them by construction: N throwaway containers produce N first-sightings and N spawns. A-30 additionally has no predicate distinguishing a long-lived service container (where rising RSS over time IS the signal) from a short-lived batch container (where high RSS is the expected shape of the job and says nothing about a leak).",
    evidence: "system-auditor signal sys-20260825T133632-2f9d, drained to PO's durable inbox as envelope 786b3b37...: 'A-30 mem_creep pre-gate has no ephemeral-container discriminator - 3 test harnesses paged the auditor in 13 min'. The 3 harnesses were the ephemeral `docker compose run --rm` containers dev-pdf-extractor used for the 2026-08-25 OCR sentinel measurement — i.e. sanctioned, bounded, throwaway work, each correctly at high RSS for the duration of a 46-page OCR job.",
    ac: "(AC-1) A-30 must classify container lifecycle before it evaluates creep, and skip (or evaluate under a different rule) containers that are not long-lived services. Derive the class from something durable — membership in docker-compose.yml's service set, or the container's own labels — never from a name-shape regex, which is the same unbounded-string trap one layer down. (AC-2) DO NOT 'fix' this by resetting spawn_count/first_seen_at or GC-ing the debounce ledger: that regresses QA-verified AC-4 and is test-locked at auditor-tier1-probe.test.sh T-DEBOUNCE-3. A change that makes that test fail is a rejection. (AC-3) POSITIVE CONTROL: with the fix in place, run three ephemeral `docker compose run --rm` containers at high RSS and show ZERO A-30 spawns. (AC-4) NEGATIVE CONTROL, non-substitutable: show A-30 still fires on a genuine long-lived-service creep — a discriminator that silences the check is strictly worse than the noise it removes (feedback_composite_score_masks_dead_detector_pruned_table).",
    status_note: "Triaged from PO durable-inbox envelope 786b3b37... (Pipeline B signal_feedback, WARN). Distinct from the three neighbouring A-30 rows: FIX-AUDITOR-A30-PROBE-SH-MISSES-RAG-SERVICE-CONTAINER is about which containers are scanned, FIX-AUDITOR-A30-CRASHCLIFF-BRANCH-CANNOT-BE-A-CRASH-BY-CONSTRUCTION is about verdict-branch labelling, FIX-AUDITOR-PREGATE-VERDICT-DIVERGENCE-MEMCREEP-NO-OWNING-CHECK is about pre-gate/cycle-verdict divergence. This row is about container-lifecycle classification and debounce key cardinality.",
    dedup_checked: "2026-08-25T13:40Z via scripts/po-board-dedup-search.sh for /mem_creep|A-30|ephemeral.*container/ -> 8 hits, all read; the 3 A-30 rows above were compared field-by-field and none covers lifecycle classification or key cardinality.",
    related: ["FIX-AUDITOR-A30-PROBE-SH-MISSES-RAG-SERVICE-CONTAINER", "FIX-AUDITOR-A30-CRASHCLIFF-BRANCH-CANNOT-BE-A-CRASH-BY-CONSTRUCTION", "FIX-AUDITOR-PREGATE-VERDICT-DIVERGENCE-MEMCREEP-NO-OWNING-CHECK", "FIX-AUDITOR-TIER1-FOLD-VERDICT-NOT-DURABLE-RESPAWNS-AUDITOR-EVERY-TICK"],
    baseline_pass: null
  })

# ── 7. bctc-discover stale pending backlog ────────────────────────────────────
| add_row({
    id: "FIX-BCTC-DISCOVER-513-STALE-PENDING-RECORDS-OVER-72H",
    type: "FIX", size: "M", priority: "P1", status: "BACKLOG",
    zone: "apps/mcp-server/", owner: "po", next_agent: "dev-mcp-server",
    created_at: $now, created_by: $by, updated_at: $now, updated_by: "po",
    dedup_key: "data_stale:bctc-discover|513-pending-over-72h",
    files: ["apps/mcp-server/src/"],
    title: "bctc-discover has 513 pending records older than 72h — a discovery queue that admits work faster than anything drains it, with no age-based escalation or terminal disposition",
    root_cause: "UNDIAGNOSED — this row exists to get it diagnosed, not to assert a cause. The auditor reports the symptom only. Candidate mechanisms to discriminate between, in order of cheapness: (a) the drain consumer is dead or throttled; (b) the drain runs but every attempt fails and the records are re-queued as pending rather than terminalised; (c) discovery admits records for reports that can never be fetched (geo-blocked / delisted / no PDF) and nothing ever marks them terminal. These have different fixes and (b) vs (c) are distinguishable purely from the records' own retry/error columns.",
    evidence: "system-auditor signal, PO durable inbox envelope b2827e04..., 2026-08-25T12:16:06Z, severity WARN: 'bctc-discover: 513 stale pending records (>72h)'. PO dedup-searched all non-terminal lanes for /bctc.?discover/ and /stale pending/ -> NO MATCH: this feed has never had a board row, so the 513 is a floor with no owner, not a known-and-tracked backlog.",
    ac: "(AC-1) FIRST re-measure independently against the live container DB, not the host DB file — the host copy is a known stale decoy that has already manufactured one false CRITICAL on this board (see FIX-AUDITOR-C01-DAILY-OHLCV-MEASURES-STALE-HOST-DB-DECOY-FALSE-CRITICAL). If the live count is materially different, correct the premise in this row before doing anything else. (AC-2) Report the age histogram and the distinct error/retry states of the 513, and name which of (a)/(b)/(c) above the data supports. A fix proposed before this is stated is a rejection. (AC-3) Whatever the cause, the queue must gain a terminal disposition for records that cannot succeed, so the pending count is bounded rather than monotonic. (AC-4) POSITIVE CONTROL: after the fix, the >72h pending count is measured again from the live container DB and is materially lower, with the drop attributed to real completions vs terminalisations separately — collapsing both into one number would let a mass-terminalisation masquerade as recovery (that exact shape is on record in SPIKE-BCTC-EXTRACTION-DORMANT-MASS-ENRICHFAIL-FLOOD).",
    status_note: "Triaged from PO durable inbox 2026-08-25T13:45Z. WARN severity but P1: 513 records over 72h is a standing coverage hole in the BCTC pipeline, which is the pipeline the standing user goal is about.",
    dedup_checked: "2026-08-25T13:40Z via scripts/po-board-dedup-search.sh for /bctc.?discover/ and /stale pending/ -> NO MATCH on non-terminal board rows.",
    related: ["FIX-AUDITOR-C01-DAILY-OHLCV-MEASURES-STALE-HOST-DB-DECOY-FALSE-CRITICAL", "FIX-REFINEBCTC-SKIPSET-NO-STATUS-FILTER-FAILED-UNITS-PERMANENTLY-TERMINAL"],
    baseline_pass: null
  })

# ── 8. CADRAT-3 pre-check gate window is commit-counted ───────────────────────
| add_row({
    id: "FIX-CADRAT3-PRECHECK-GATE-WINDOW-COMMIT-COUNTED-NOT-TIME-BOUNDED",
    type: "FIX", size: "S", priority: "P1", status: "BACKLOG",
    zone: "cross-service/", owner: "po", next_agent: "agent-father",
    created_at: $now, created_by: $by, updated_at: $now, updated_by: "po",
    dedup_key: "cadrat3:pre-check-gate-window-commit-counted-head3",
    files: ["docs/agents/agent-father/flow/main.md"],
    title: "Every CADRAT-3 Pre-Check gate asks 'did an in-scope file change in git diff HEAD~3..HEAD' — a COMMIT-count window, not a time window. At 266 commits/day that spans ~2 minutes, so a once-daily cron is really asking 'did this change in the last two minutes?' and near-always gets no, making the gated primary function effectively dead code",
    root_cause: "HEAD~3 is a fixed commit count. Its wall-clock span is inversely proportional to repo commit rate, and this repo's rate is high and rising (266 commits on 2026-08-25 alone). The gate was presumably written when three commits meant hours. At the observed rate the window measured 14:46:14 -> 14:48:10 = 116 seconds at agent-father's own gate-eval moment. Any cron whose cadence exceeds that window is structurally guaranteed to see 'no in-scope change' and skip its own primary function on nearly every run.",
    evidence: "Router signal router-20260825T131500-gatewindow, observed by router session c6581d0a-1104-40e4-8b55-16c563969d28 during agent-father keep-cycle 2026-08-25T13:01Z, delivered to PO's durable inbox twice (envelopes 28ec4ef5... file-sourced and d0474cf6... dashboard-sourced — one incident, two transports). The 116-second window and the 266-commit day are both stated as measured at gate-eval time.",
    ac: "(AC-1) Enumerate EVERY CADRAT-3 Pre-Check gate before changing any of them and report the count — the signal says 'all' of them, and a point-fix on the one gate that happened to be observed leaves the class open, which is a rejection. (AC-2) Replace the commit-count window with a window whose span is a function of the CRON'S OWN CADENCE, not of repo commit rate: `git log --since` against the cadence period, or the gate's own last-run timestamp. State which and why. (AC-3) POSITIVE CONTROL: with the fix in place and a matching in-scope file changed 12h before the run, a once-daily cron's gate must OPEN. (AC-4) NEGATIVE CONTROL: with no in-scope change inside the cadence period, it must still SKIP — this fix must not degrade into an always-open gate, which would just move the waste rather than remove it. (AC-5) Report, for each gate found in AC-1, how many of its recent runs would have flipped outcome under the fix — that number is the actual cost of the bug and belongs on the record.",
    status_note: "Triaged from PO durable inbox 2026-08-25T13:45Z (2 duplicate envelopes, one incident). Routed to agent-father: docs/agents/**/flow/*.md is instruction-prose per the 2026-07-21 PO artifact-class routing ruling. WARN severity but P1 — a silently-skipped primary function on a daily cron is invisible by construction and this is the first time it has been measured rather than assumed.",
    dedup_checked: "2026-08-25T13:40Z via scripts/po-board-dedup-search.sh for /CADRAT|HEAD~3|gate window/ -> NO MATCH on non-terminal board rows.",
    related: [],
    baseline_pass: null
  })

